caption: Universal engine
engine-rule: universal-engine

Every spell is an individual skill.

The character must know all prerequisites before learning a spell normally.

A Class may bypass the instructor and Domain-entry requirements, but does not grant unknown prerequisite spells for free.

Class Tradition access: When a Regular Tradition is selected as a Class Tradition, the character may learn without an instructor any spell accessible through that Tradition that has both a prerequisite count of 1 or less and a Magery or Power Investiture requirement of 1 or less. This does not expand the Tradition’s legal spell scope, grant prerequisite spells for free, or waive ordinary character-point costs, casting rules, energy costs, or failure rules. An individual Tradition may explicitly narrow, broaden, replace, or otherwise alter this Class Tradition access rule.

The Tradition defines which colleges or spells are legal.

Casting otherwise uses normal spell rules plus the Domain’s energy and failure rules.
